kora=hero('Kora','A personal AI assistant with a place for your context, tools, and work.','<span>December 2025 — Present</span><span>Personal project · Public source</span><span>React / Tauri / TypeScript / SQLite</span>',link('Explore the demo','#demo',True)+link('View source',GH))
kora+=f'''<section class="shell demo-section" id="demo"><div class="demo-heading"><div><h2>Meet your other workspace.</h2><p>Explore a fictional day in Kora. Browse work, open a conversation, and follow the context.</p></div><span class="demo-disclosure">Interactive sample · No live AI</span></div><div class="demo-embed" data-embed="/demos/kora/#/kora"><div class="demo-cover">{image('/assets/projects/kora-interactive-sample.png','Preview of the interactive Kora sample',eager=True)}<div class="demo-cover-action"><button class="action action--primary" data-load-demo>Open interactive demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p>Uses fictional data. No account needed.</p></div></div></div><div class="demo-caption"><p>The demo adapts Kora’s real UI components for the browser. Actions change sample data only.</p><a href="/demos/kora/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open in a full window ↗</a></div></section>'''
kora+=section('A personal assistant needs more than a chat box.','<p class="lead">The useful part is continuity: knowing what you are working on, finding the relevant context, and keeping the result somewhere you can use it again.</p><p>Kora brings conversations, personal knowledge, and structured work into a Windows application. A shared runtime connects the desktop interface, CLI, and Chrome extension, with durable state in SQLite.</p>')
kora+=section('What I built.','''<div class="decision-list"><article><h3>One runtime, several ways in.</h3><p>I extended Pi’s open-source foundation with Kora’s tools, skills, personal context, and product services. The interfaces share behavior rather than each implementing a separate assistant.</p></article><article><h3>Context with somewhere to live.</h3><p>Persistent records and hybrid retrieval connect the assistant to personal knowledge and work. Keeping state locally makes it inspectable; model requests still use the configured provider.</p></article><article><h3>Work that can continue.</h3><p>Durable sessions and stored artifacts give the assistant a way to pick up existing work instead of starting every interaction from scratch.</p></article></div>''')
kora+=section('Follow the architecture.',f'''<div class="flow-diagram"><div><b>Desktop · CLI · Browser</b><p>Interfaces for the same assistant</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><div><b>Kora runtime</b><p>Pi foundation · tools & skills · context · sessions</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><div><b>Persistent state & connected tools</b><p>SQLite · personal knowledge · files · permitted actions</p></div></div><p><a class="text-link" href="/work-writing/kora-runtime/">Read the engineering walkthrough ↗</a></p>''')
kora+=section('Test the messy parts.','''<p class="lead">What happens when a plan changes halfway through the week?</p><p>I built an evaluation harness with simulated-user interactions, controlled event timing, changing workweek scenarios, and blinded review. It examines task completion, memory persistence, authorization boundaries, and recovery across restarts.</p><div class="scenario"><h3>A changing week</h3><ol><li>A person gives the assistant plans and constraints.</li><li>New information changes what is feasible.</li><li>A later interaction tests whether the assistant kept the right context.</li><li>The review inspects the actual outcome, including missed work and recovery.</li></ol></div><p>This is ongoing evaluation work. The interactive sample above demonstrates the interface; it does not run this evaluation or make a live agent request.</p>''')
kora+=section('Built in the open.',f'<p>Kora is in active development. The public repository contains the Windows app, runtime, and setup instructions, including its Pi-derived foundation and license notices.</p>{link("Explore the repository",GH,True)}')
page('/projects/kora/','Kora — Personal AI','Explore Kora’s interactive sample and the engineering behind a local-first Windows AI assistant.',kora)

ks=hero('KS App','People and an AI operator, working on the same business records.','<span>May 2026 — Present</span><span>Private project · In development</span><span>Next.js / TypeScript / PostgreSQL / Supabase</span>',link('Explore a workflow','#workspace',True))
ks+='''<section class="shell demo-section" id="workspace"><div class="demo-heading"><div><h2>From client context to the next action.</h2><p>Select a project, inspect its context, and prepare a sample update.</p></div><span class="demo-disclosure">Interactive illustration · Fictional records</span></div><div class="ks-sample" data-ks-sample><div class="ks-sample-sidebar"><strong>Northstar Studio</strong><p>Project workspace</p><label for="project-search">Find a project</label><input id="project-search" type="search" placeholder="Search sample projects"><div class="sample-project-list"><button class="sample-project active" data-project="website" aria-pressed="true">Website refresh<span>Juniper Wellness</span></button><button class="sample-project" data-project="brand" aria-pressed="false">Brand guidelines<span>Cedar & Co.</span></button><button class="sample-project" data-project="onboarding" aria-pressed="false">Client onboarding<span>Northstar Studio</span></button></div><p class="no-projects" hidden>No matching projects.</p></div><div class="ks-sample-content"><div class="sample-title"><span class="status" data-project-status>In progress</span><button class="text-button" data-reset-sample>Reset sample ↺</button></div><h3 data-project-title>Website refresh</h3><p data-project-client>Juniper Wellness · Client delivery</p><div class="sample-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Project view"><button aria-pressed="true" data-sample-tab="overview">Overview</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-sample-tab="activity">Activity</button></div><div data-sample-overview><h4>The next milestone</h4><p data-project-detail>Review the homepage direction with the client, then prepare the remaining service pages.</p><div class="sample-task"><input id="sample-task" type="checkbox"><label for="sample-task">Review the latest project notes</label></div><button class="action action--primary" data-prepare-update>Prepare sample update <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><div data-sample-activity hidden><p data-activity-empty>No changes in this sample yet.</p><ul data-activity-list></ul></div><div class="sample-draft" hidden aria-live="polite"><h4>Draft client update</h4><p data-draft-text></p><span>Prepared locally from fictional records. Nothing has been sent.</span></div></div></div><p class="media-caption">This portfolio illustration explains the workflow using local sample data. It is not the live KS App interface or an executing AI agent.</p></section>'''
ks+=section('A connected business workspace.','<p class="lead">Client information should travel with the work.</p><p>KS App brings CRM, project delivery, finance, knowledge, and client portals into one workspace. Its AI operator uses the same domain services as the human interface, so a request is grounded in the application’s records and permissions.</p>')
ks+=section('The engineering underneath.','''<div class="decision-list"><article><h3>Permissions belong to the application.</h3><p>Workspace identity and allowed operations come from server-owned context. The model does not get to choose its tenant, role, or credentials.</p></article><article><h3>Skills guide. Tools act.</h3><p>Versioned skill guidance and on-demand tool discovery expose the operations needed for the work. Tools call shared business services instead of inventing a second data layer.</p></article><article><h3>Keep the record of what happened.</h3><p>Persistent conversations, durable workflows, approvals, and action receipts support recovery after interruptions. Uncertain external actions need reconciliation before another attempt.</p></article></div>''')
ks+=section('One action, one set of rules.','''<div class="flow-diagram"><div><b>Person or AI operator</b><p>Request a business operation</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><div><b>Shared domain services</b><p>Workspace identity · permissions · approvals</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><div><b>Records & action history</b><p>PostgreSQL / Supabase · persisted outcomes · recovery</p></div></div>''')
ks+=section('Where it stands.','<p>KS App is an active private development project. The source implements the workspace and operator architecture; complete release qualification and production readiness remain ongoing. The sample is designed to make its product model understandable without exposing a client workspace.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/commercial-work/">See my shipped client work ↗</a></p>')
page('/projects/ks-app/','KS App — Business workspace','A multi-tenant business platform with shared services for people and an AI operator. Explore an illustrated workflow.',ks)

