world=hero('WorldBuilder','Exploring the engineering of worlds that can grow without losing their history.','<span>Ongoing project</span><span>Domain modeling / TypeScript / PostgreSQL</span>')
world+='''<section class="shell world-intro"><p class="world-question">A world changes.<br><span>What should stay true?</span></p><p>WorldBuilder investigates that question through structured generation, immutable content, and durable state.</p></section>'''
world+=section('The idea.','<p class="lead">A generated world should have more than a collection of disconnected answers.</p><p>I’m exploring how creative direction can become structured world data with clear identities, traceable revisions, and a workflow that can continue over time.</p>')
world+=section('The current implementation.','<div class="decision-list"><article><h3>Seed-to-Frame domain</h3><p>A pure domain layer defines the initial structured world model and its rules.</p></article><article><h3>Durable content</h3><p>Immutable bodies and PostgreSQL-backed state separate large content from the records that coordinate work.</p></article><article><h3>Provider composition</h3><p>Codex SDK composition and an authentication verifier prepare the integration boundary. Current runtime exercises are scripted.</p></article></div>')
world+=section('What is still being built.','<p>The current version does not yet provide a complete generation workflow, live model dispatch, or downstream world products. I’m keeping the project here as a record of engineering exploration, with the implementation distinguished from the intended experience.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/kora/">Explore Kora, my featured AI project ↗</a></p>')
page('/projects/worldbuilder/','WorldBuilder — Work in progress','An ongoing exploration of structured world generation, immutable content, and durable state.',world)

